# frame: 2 F-M1
# frame: 5 F-M2
# frame: 8 F-M3
# program: fixtures/FX-diag-stic-2/diag-stic-2.listing.txt (ivs-diag-stic-2), entered through the
#   project boot stub contract 2 (boot-stub-2: cartridge reset entry 5000, interrupt entry 5004), with
#   the zero graphics ROM and no EXEC image
#
# Predicate of ivs-diag-stic-2 with KEY_1 closed from tick 0, the selector byte 7E (plan 08-07, D-04, D-05,
#   D-10): the guest words at the one bound (marker 03C5, the frame counter 000A, the selector word 007E, the
#   scene number 0003 of the last routine), frame 0 not displayed, frames 2 and 8 displayed, the three scene
#   pictures by hash (frame 2 F-M1, one MOB at double width clipped at the right and bottom edges; frame 5 F-M2,
#   three MOBs with an X flip, a Y flip and both, at four plane rows per pattern row; frame 8 F-M3, priority
#   between MOBs, a MOB over a card, the color bit and eight plane rows per pattern row) and nine pixel probes,
#   and ten delivered frames, all derived by hand in docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md (sections (a) to (f);
#   the frame literals data/video/frames/F-M*.frame with their sha256-text keys) BEFORE the program, its
#   listing, the scenario or any run existed (oracle commit 641a12e3a1059b242cc88a3ee4308e3f58d9b36d, blind
#   second read closed in commit 9250265), and copied here line for line from the committed block. It was not
#   generated by, read back from or edited to match the core or a run. The author of this derivation also wrote
#   the literals, the STIC rules, the program and the core, and the blind reader is of the same model family, so
#   all of them can share one misreading of a source; agreement among them is not independent evidence about
#   hardware.
# The three scenes change at the routines of frames 4 and 7, so the asserted frames 2, 5 and 8 are the middle
#   frame of each scene, one frame from each change, and no frame assert names frame 0 or frame 1 (the settling
#   rule of the derivation, section (b); the input is applied at tick 0).
# Excluded on purpose: machine time (printed in the report, never asserted), the stack word [0340] (C68),
# all CPU registers, R7 and the flags (C40, C45, C56), and every pinned item of the derivation, section
# (i): the pixels of a MOB with the priority bit set (PD-1), half-height pixels (PD-2), a collision of a MOB
# at X coordinate 0 (PD-3), the border bit of a collision register (PD-4), a collision outside the plane
# (PD-5), a collision in a frame with the display off (PD-6), the read and clear semantics of the collision
# registers beyond sticky bits and a write of zero (PD-7), the height unit of the top strip (PD-8), a strip
# against the delay (PD-9), the content of the area a delay exposes and a MOB in it (PD-10, PD-11), the delay
# range (PD-12), and the bus windows against the vertical delay (PD-13).
# Body: one assert per clause in the runner's scenario grammar, hex upper case, exact compare, evaluated
# at the end of the step above it, in the order of data/scenarios/diag-stic2-mob-pass.ivss
# (golden-expect-drift). The step line below is a comment.
# step: run-to 640000 ticks
